    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0491" n="479" xml:id="pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/6431: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-21T21:00:00+02:00">August 21, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 22—2:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1159. My 1149, August 20, 10 p.m. If Orgaz has not yet forwarded <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to Madrid I believe it would be
                    advisable for Childs to amend it by omitting last paragraph substance of which
                    could be conveyed to General Orgaz orally. I am sure Childs could give a
                    reasonable explanation of his action.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tangier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
